      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>topics/supported-audio-formats.dita</code></strong> <code>id="choosing"</code> on the section makes it a link target. The related links include an external one with <code>@scope="external"</code>, <code>@format="html"</code> and its own <code>&lt;linktext&gt;</code>, because there is no DITA title to take the text from.
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\n+++ b/topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\n@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@\n       \u003cterm>Lossless\u003c/term> formats keep every sample of the source; \u003cterm>lossy\u003c/term> formats discard detail to make smaller files.\n       Exported files are named after the project, so \u003cfilepath>podcast-episode-1.aup3\u003c/filepath> exports as \u003cfilepath>podcast-episode-1.mp3\u003c/filepath>.\u003c/p>\n     \u003c/section>\n-    \u003csection>\n+    \u003csection id=\"choosing\">\n       \u003ctitle>Choosing a format\u003c/title>\n       \u003cp>Keep a lossless master and export a lossy copy for distribution:\u003c/p>\n       \u003col>\n@@ -70,4 +70,10 @@\n       \u003c/tgroup>\n     \u003c/table>\n   \u003c/refbody>\n+  \u003crelated-links>\n+    \u003clink href=\"exporting-audio.dita\"/>\n+    \u003clink href=\"https://manual.audacityteam.org/man/file_formats.html\" scope=\"external\" format=\"html\">\n+      \u003clinktext>File formats in the Audacity Manual\u003c/linktext>\n+    \u003c/link>\n+  \u003c/related-links>\n \u003c/reference>"} lang="diff" title="topics/supported-audio-formats.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the elements</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;xref href="…"/&gt;</code> with no content: output supplies the target's <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> as the link text. This is the usual form for a link to a DITA topic, and it updates the link text when the target title changes.</li>
      <li><code>href="file.dita"</code> links to the topic. <code>href="file.dita#topic/element"</code> links to an element inside it that has an <code>@id</code>; the topic id is required in the fragment because one file can hold several topics.</li>
      <li><code>@scope="external"</code> says the target is outside the project and is not to be resolved or copied. <code>@format="html"</code> says what kind of thing it is, so the processor does not try to parse it as DITA.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;link&gt;</code> is the same reference as <code>&lt;xref&gt;</code> but as a list entry in <code>&lt;related-links&gt;</code>. It takes <code>&lt;linktext&gt;</code> for the text when the target has no title, and <code>&lt;desc&gt;</code> for a short description shown under the link.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-2-related-links-on-the-remaining-topics" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 2: Related links on the remaining topics<a href="#step-2-related-links-on-the-remaining-topics" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>topics/recording-your-first-track.dita</code></strong> A cross-reference in the context, a new <code>&lt;postreq&gt;</code> with two links, and a <code>&lt;related-links&gt;</code> block after <code>&lt;/taskbody&gt;</code>.
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\n+++ b/topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\n@@ -7,7 +7,8 @@\n   \u003ctaskbody>\n     \u003ccontext>\n       \u003cp>This task walks you through making your first audio recording.\n-      You need a microphone connected to your computer.\u003c/p>\n+      You need a microphone connected to your computer.\n+      If you are new to audio terms such as sample rate and clipping, read \u003cxref href=\"what-is-digital-audio.dita\"/> first.\u003c/p>\n       \u003cnote type=\"tip\">For best results, record in a quiet room and position the microphone 15 to 30 cm from your mouth.\u003c/note>\n     \u003c/context>\n     \u003csteps>\n@@ -46,5 +47,12 @@\n       \u003cp>You now have a recorded audio track in your project.\n       The waveform shows the shape of the recorded audio: louder sounds appear as taller waves.\u003c/p>\n     \u003c/result>\n+    \u003cpostreq>\n+      \u003cp>Trim the false starts (\u003cxref href=\"trimming-audio.dita\"/>), then export the result (\u003cxref href=\"exporting-audio.dita\"/>).\u003c/p>\n+    \u003c/postreq>\n   \u003c/taskbody>\n+  \u003crelated-links>\n+    \u003clink href=\"preparing-to-record.dita\"/>\n+    \u003clink href=\"removing-background-noise.dita\"/>\n+  \u003c/related-links>\n \u003c/task>"} lang="diff" title="topics/recording-your-first-track.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>topics/trimming-audio.dita</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/trimming-audio.dita\n+++ b/topics/trimming-audio.dita\n@@ -45,4 +45,8 @@\n       \u003cp>The unwanted audio is gone and the track plays through without a gap.\u003c/p>\n     \u003c/result>\n   \u003c/taskbody>\n+  \u003crelated-links>\n+    \u003clink href=\"recording-your-first-track.dita\"/>\n+    \u003clink href=\"exporting-audio.dita\"/>\n+  \u003c/related-links>\n \u003c/task>"} lang="diff" title="topics/trimming-audio.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>topics/what-is-audacity.dita</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/what-is-audacity.dita\n+++ b/topics/what-is-audacity.dita\n@@ -22,4 +22,12 @@\n       Whatever the project, Audacity provides the tools at no cost.\u003c/p>\n     \u003c/section>\n   \u003c/conbody>\n+  \u003crelated-links>\n+    \u003clink href=\"what-is-digital-audio.dita\"/>\n+    \u003clink href=\"installing-audacity.dita\"/>\n+    \u003clink href=\"https://www.audacityteam.org/\" scope=\"external\" format=\"html\">\n+      \u003clinktext>The Audacity website\u003c/linktext>\n+      \u003cdesc>Downloads, the manual and the user forum.\u003c/desc>\n+    \u003c/link>\n+  \u003c/related-links>\n \u003c/concept>"} lang="diff" title="topics/what-is-audacity.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita</code></strong> This one groups its links. A <code>&lt;linklist&gt;</code> has a <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> and keeps its links in the order written; a <code>&lt;linkpool&gt;</code> has no title and lets the processor sort and merge its links with the ones the map generates later.
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\n+++ b/topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\n@@ -6,7 +6,8 @@\n   \u003cshortdesc>Digital audio is sound stored as numbers: samples taken thousands of times a second at a chosen precision.\u003c/shortdesc>\n   \u003cconbody>\n     \u003cp>Digital audio is sound that has been converted into a numerical representation.\n-    A few key concepts help you make better recordings and edits.\u003c/p>\n+    A few key concepts help you make better recordings and edits.\n+    If you would rather start recording, go straight to \u003cxref href=\"recording-your-first-track.dita\"/> and come back later.\u003c/p>\n     \u003csection>\n       \u003ctitle>Waveforms\u003c/title>\n       \u003cp>Sound travels through air as a continuous \u003cterm>waveform\u003c/term> of pressure changes.\n@@ -72,4 +73,17 @@\n       \u003clq reftitle=\"The Audacity Manual\">Audio is measured in decibels because the ear hears ratios, not differences.\u003c/lq>\n     \u003c/section>\n   \u003c/conbody>\n+  \u003crelated-links>\n+    \u003clinklist>\n+      \u003ctitle>Put it into practice\u003c/title>\n+      \u003clink href=\"recording-your-first-track.dita\"/>\n+      \u003clink href=\"preparing-to-record.dita\"/>\n+    \u003c/linklist>\n+    \u003clinkpool>\n+      \u003clink href=\"supported-audio-formats.dita\"/>\n+      \u003clink href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sampling_(signal_processing)\" scope=\"external\" format=\"html\">\n+        \u003clinktext>Sampling (signal processing)\u003c/linktext>\n+      \u003c/link>\n+    \u003c/linkpool>\n+  \u003c/related-links>\n \u003c/concept>"} lang="diff" title="topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the placement</strong> <code>&lt;related-links&gt;</code> is a child of the topic, after the body, not inside it. In a task it follows <code>&lt;/taskbody&gt;</code>; in a concept, <code>&lt;/conbody&gt;</code>. The validator rejects it anywhere else.
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-3-update-the-readme-and-run-the-gate" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 3: Update the README and run the gate<a href="#step-3-update-the-readme-and-run-the-gate" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Change the "You are on" line</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n Build a guide through 27 stages. Maps begin at stage 02; HTML publication begins at stage 03.\n \n-You are on stage 06: rich tasks.\n+You are on stage 07: links.\n \n ## Stages\n "} lang="diff" title="README.md" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Format and check</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml format -i topics/*.dita\nscripts/check-stage.sh"} lang="bash" />
      <CodeBlock code={"== validate-project  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\n9 file(s): 9 valid, 0 invalid.\n\n== project-health  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\nRoot map: none (none configured); house rules: none (none configured)\nProject is healthy: valid, no broken references, keys, orphans, or broken element ids.\n\n== build  skipped (no project.json yet) ==\n\nSTAGE OK"} lang="plaintext" />
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <p>This is the first stage where <code>project-health</code> has something to check besides validity: every <code>@href</code> now has to resolve. Misspell the target of the <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> to <em>Trimming audio</em> in <em>Exporting audio</em> as <code>trimming-audo.dita</code> and run the gate. The file still validates, because a broken link is not a grammar error, but the health check reports it and the stage fails:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"== project-health  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\nRoot map: none (none configured); house rules: none (none configured)\nBroken references (1):\n  /home/you/audacity-guide/topics/exporting-audio.dita:61  @href=\"trimming-audo.dita\"\n…\nFAIL: project-health found issues"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The validation and health checks cover different problems. A wrong fragment such as <code>#supported-audio-formats/choose</code> passes the health check and, once there is a map, the DITA-OT build as well. The link renders and points at the top of the topic instead of the section. Check fragments by clicking them in the built output. <code>dogsbay-xml conref-audit</code> checks conref target IDs; it does not replace testing these cross-reference links.</p>
      <h2 id="why-links-belong-in-the-map" class="group scroll-mt-20">Why links belong in the map<a href="#why-links-belong-in-the-map" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p>Every <code>&lt;related-links&gt;</code> block you wrote here is a statement about how topics relate, stored inside one of the two topics. When you organize the map in stage 09 and relationship tables in stage 09, those statements move to the map, where one <code>&lt;reltable&gt;</code> row says "these topics are related" once and the processor generates the links on both sides. Topics then carry only the <code>&lt;xref&gt;</code>s that the text needs, and the same topic can be related to different neighbors in different guides.</p>
      <p>Writing these links first shows the relationships that the map later generates. Topic-level links are also useful when publishing a topic on its own.</p>
      <p>After each error exercise, undo the deliberate change and rerun the gate. Confirm that it prints <code>STAGE OK</code> before continuing.</p>
      <h2 id="publish-your-changes" class="group scroll-mt-20">Publish your changes<a href="#publish-your-changes" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p>Add the lesson's topics to <code>audacity-guide.ditamap</code>, then rebuild the guide. The complete map at this checkpoint is:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003c!DOCTYPE map PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Map//EN\" \"map.dtd\">\n\n\u003cmap>\n  \u003ctitle>Audio user guide\u003c/title>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/exporting-audio.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/installing-audacity.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/preparing-to-record.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/removing-background-noise.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/trimming-audio.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/what-is-audacity.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\"/>\n\u003c/map>"} lang="xml" title="audacity-guide.ditamap" />
      <CodeBlock code={"dita --project=project.json --output=out\npython3 scripts/check-output-links.py out"} lang="bash" />
      <h2 id="what-you-learned" class="group scroll-mt-20">What you learned<a href="#what-you-learned" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;xref&gt;</code> in the text; <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> in <code>&lt;related-links&gt;</code> after the body.</li>
      <li>Empty link elements take their text from the target's title.</li>
      <li><code>file#topic/element</code> reaches a section or any element with an <code>@id</code>.</li>
      <li><code>@scope="external"</code> and <code>@format</code> for links out of the project; <code>&lt;linktext&gt;</code> when there is no title to borrow; <code>&lt;desc&gt;</code> for a blurb.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;linklist&gt;</code> keeps order and has a title; <code>&lt;linkpool&gt;</code> lets the processor sort and merge.</li>
      <li><code>project-health</code> catches broken references that validation cannot.</li>
      </ul>
